    "submission": "submission-check2.json",
    "summary": "Turn 13 extended the reviewed scenario to the accept round on the same unit and obligation, so the confirmed finding's consequence gets its own oracle.\n\nState on entry. The direct check for C1-recovery-adopts-committed-vector is now confirmed in scope: outcome violated, comparison_observed true, reviewed_complete true with correspondence no_issue_found, and no open issues. The remaining question I carried from the review was what happens after the non-adopting resolution: the recoverer enters the accept phase, and the only replica that can answer is the one that already committed the instance.\n\nNew artifact (not a repair). The harness now follows that accept round: the Accept the resolution emitted is delivered to the committed replica and its AcceptReply is delivered back to the recoverer, and the harness emits a canonical accept_round_after_commit event carrying accept_oks_before/after, reply_counted, instance_status_after and committed_at_recoverer. The local construction run showed accept_oks 0 to 0, reply_counted false, instance_status_after ACCEPTED and committed_at_recoverer false, which matches the source reading that handleAccept on an already-COMMITTED record refuses to store the new attributes and answers with its own bal, after which handleAcceptReply drops the reply on the lastTriedBallot check. The plan adds a second monitor and an event_assertion that the committed replica's reply must be counted, with the committed_reply prerequisite retained as admission alias and identity correlation, plus an uncertainty noting that the periodic re-trigger and the eventual row state are not modelled. The harness content stays in the submitted file and the plan keeps the reviewed artifact's basis intact, so the original violated witness is untouched while this consequence is checked on fresh bytes and a fresh execution.\n\nScope honesty. The added property is bounded to one accept attempt for one instance: it records that the recovery has no live continuation through the committed replica's reply, not that the row is permanently blocked. No map object was changed, and no requirement, premise or earlier observation was weakened."
